  "id": "synchrony",
  "term": "synchrony",
  "definition": "Synchrony, in this social context, means two people spontaneously coordinating their movements in time with each other. It is linked with social bonding, collaboration, and rapport, and may be more likely after cooperative interaction or when initial rapport is stronger.",
